{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $(0,16)$ such that $f'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $f$ over the interval:\n\n$f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(16)-f(0)}{(16)-(0)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{f(16)-f(0)}{(16)-(0)}=\\dfrac{5-3}{16}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{8}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $f$ and find the $x$-value for which $f'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{8}}$.\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+9}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{8}$ is $x=7$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=7$ is indeed within the interval $(0,16)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{x+9}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x+9)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(x+9)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x+9)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+9}}(1)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+9}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{8}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+9}}\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{8}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{x+9}\u0026=4\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{x+9})^2\u0026=4^2\n\\\\\\\\\nx+9\u0026=16\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=7\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=7$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+9}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $f$ on the interval $[0,16]$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$16$","correct":false},{"content":"$43$","correct":false},{"content":"$55$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$7$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
